{:edb/db-before-t 811 :edb/db-after-t 812 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534124 50 #inst "2026-10-06T03:48:03.815Z" 13194139534124 true] [17592186092114 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277990 13194139534124 true] [17592186092114 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277995 13194139534124 true] [17592186092116 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278002 13194139534124 true] [17592186092117 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277979 13194139534124 true] [17592186092117 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277986 13194139534124 true] [17592186277979 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277980 13194139534124 true] [17592186277979 1089 "q-121542" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277979 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534124 true] [17592186277979 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977868/assets/56726fc8331106df9b20aed561a2ed3b93fe12d90da85a8d1b92e610b19033f7.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and the line $y=\\sqrt{3}.$ Find the $x$-coordinate of the point $B.$\n\n$$\n\n$$" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277979 1113 #uuid "40f7d319-bfe9-5828-b013-a9a68e7eb115" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277979 1145 "The $y$-values of both functions are the same at the intersection point. Equating the two equations gives: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\sqrt{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})=\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis value lies outside $-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}<x<-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ To get a value that's inside the required domain, we add $-\\pi $  to the principal value. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=-\\pi +x=-\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{3}=-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the $x$-coordinate of $B$ is $-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.$" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277980 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277981 13194139534124 true] [17592186277980 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277982 13194139534124 true] [17592186277980 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277983 13194139534124 true] [17592186277980 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277984 13194139534124 true] [17592186277980 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277985 13194139534124 true] [17592186277980 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534124 true] [17592186277980 1041 "selection" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277980 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277985 13194139534124 true] [17592186277980 1110 #uuid "47929783-18a2-5a5a-918b-3a7c899616ea" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277981 1034 "-\\frac{6\\pi }{5}" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277981 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534124 true] [17592186277981 1111 #uuid "64665c65-a217-51f5-8b50-4ce3d6c2bc6c" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277982 1034 "-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277982 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534124 true] [17592186277982 1111 #uuid "49bce2c0-7111-5786-8d41-c1887b6cb48d" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277983 1034 "-\\frac{8\\pi }{7}" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277983 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534124 true] [17592186277983 1111 #uuid "e69e16d0-fee5-54d3-a02b-cc2ee311af9d" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277984 1034 "-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277984 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534124 true] [17592186277984 1111 #uuid "fc9eb9a0-3d07-5668-ac3e-e9d02100b319" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277985 1034 "-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277985 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534124 true] [17592186277985 1111 #uuid "6d57f986-db13-514b-ab92-c979718aa86d" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277986 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277987 13194139534124 true] [17592186277986 1089 "q-274852" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277986 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534124 true] [17592186277986 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977868/assets/047f02622fc176fee8c6cb0e81a0434ee208648dca14102b1d96e37b901d51f2.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and the line $y=1.$\n\nThe **exact** value of the $x$-coordinate of the point $A$ is \n{{field-1}}." 13194139534124 true] [17592186277986 1113 #uuid "d180bdf2-fe1c-5547-a6bb-3dbae8427806" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277986 1145 "The $y$-values of both functions are the same at the intersection point. Equating the two equations gives:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis value lies outside $-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}<x<-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ To get a value that's inside the required domain, we add $-\\pi $ to the principal value. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =x+(-\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\pi  \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the $x$-coordinate of $A$ is $-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.$" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277987 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277988 13194139534124 true] [17592186277987 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277989 13194139534124 true] [17592186277987 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534124 true] [17592186277987 1041 "field-1" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277987 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277989 13194139534124 true] [17592186277987 1110 #uuid "8e829784-352e-546b-b589-dc5d8deeeb5f" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277988 1034 "-\\frac{\\pi}{4}" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277988 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534124 true] [17592186277988 1111 #uuid "94f8b14f-8fe0-527f-b3be-dfaee31315b4" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277989 1034 "-\\frac{3\\pi}{4}" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277989 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534124 true] [17592186277989 1111 #uuid "bfdf1082-baca-55f0-b3c8-148cd49f2361" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277990 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277991 13194139534124 true] [17592186277990 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277993 13194139534124 true] [17592186277990 1089 "q-321622" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277990 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534124 true] [17592186277990 1100 "Find the solutions **in degrees** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{1}{6}$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ Round your answers to **the nearest integer**.\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$ and $x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277990 1113 #uuid "64dbab80-af43-59e4-8d97-d949c8f2ff4d" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277990 1145 "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=arctan\\,(\\frac{1}{6})=9.4623{…}^{∘}≈{9}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${9}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={9}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={180}^{∘}+9.4623{…}^{∘}≈{189}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order and rounded to the nearest integer, the solutions are $x={9}^{∘}$ and $x={189}^{∘}.$" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277991 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277992 13194139534124 true] [17592186277991 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534124 true] [17592186277991 1041 "field-1" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277991 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277992 13194139534124 true] [17592186277991 1110 #uuid "86ac4f73-8253-5b38-8431-20e467ca1ad5" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277992 1034 "9" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277992 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534124 true] [17592186277992 1111 #uuid "95d4ea44-d1c7-5a57-8c4b-c552f9b48ea9" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277993 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277994 13194139534124 true] [17592186277993 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534124 true] [17592186277993 1041 "field-2" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277993 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277994 13194139534124 true] [17592186277993 1110 #uuid "4104241c-1ccd-5359-ad5b-f7628f4def96" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277994 1034 "189" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277994 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534124 true] [17592186277994 1111 #uuid "32b9adcf-ccbb-577c-b00a-654888926547" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277995 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277996 13194139534124 true] [17592186277995 1089 "q-72824" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277995 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534124 true] [17592186277995 1100 "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-8$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to one decimal place?" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277995 1113 #uuid "63edf08b-7802-5b9f-940f-83ad72d838db" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277995 1145 "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-8)=-1.446\\,4…≈-1.446\\,4.\n$$\n\nSince $-1.446\\,4$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\pi -1.446\\,4≈1.695\\,2, \\\\ {x}_{2} & =2\\pi -1.446\\,4≈4.836\\,8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈1.695\\,2\\cdot 4.836\\,8≈8.2\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." 13194139534124 true] [17592186277996 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277997 13194139534124 true] [17592186277996 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277998 13194139534124 true] [17592186277996 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277999 13194139534124 true] [17592186277996 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278000 13194139534124 true] [17592186277996 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278001 13194139534124 true] [17592186277996 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534124 true] [17592186277996 1041 "selection" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277996 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277999 13194139534124 true] [17592186277996 1110 #uuid "3b4d9ab4-51c5-5dc6-a7af-e60ea74a4d13" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277997 1034 "7.8" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277997 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534124 true] [17592186277997 1111 #uuid "6dbe7c01-e369-57d3-b4d3-2aa7b3f424bd" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277998 1034 "0.8" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277998 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534124 true] [17592186277998 1111 #uuid "4849510a-f2db-5905-a715-d49ffc472fc8" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277999 1034 "8.2" 13194139534124 true] [17592186277999 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534124 true] [17592186277999 1111 #uuid "85239dd0-8edd-577c-be8d-3ad4a247bfda" 13194139534124 true] [17592186278000 1034 "8.4" 13194139534124 true] [17592186278000 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534124 true] [17592186278000 1111 #uuid "daa3bbb7-7a62-5f02-a7c0-0b9268fa6df3" 13194139534124 true] [17592186278001 1034 "8.0" 13194139534124 true] [17592186278001 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534124 true] [17592186278001 1111 #uuid "561aca6a-b656-5ddc-bdc5-5fb329ac7b18" 13194139534124 true] [17592186278002 1017 #edb/ref 17592186278003 13194139534124 true] [17592186278002 1089 "q-8720" 13194139534124 true] [17592186278002 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534124 true] [17592186278002 1100 "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-5\\sqrt{3}=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" 13194139534124 true] [17592186278002 1113 #uuid "417331c2-762c-5bf7-9ba6-a204c035e2e5" 13194139534124 true] [17592186278002 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-5\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ 5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =5\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})=\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=-\\pi +{x}_{1}=-\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{3}=-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{2\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{2\\pi }{3})=-\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{9}.\n$$" 13194139534124 true] [17592186278003 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278004 13194139534124 true] [17592186278003 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278005 13194139534124 true] [17592186278003 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278006 13194139534124 true] [17592186278003 1000 #edb/ref 175921862